# cFish.io Development Steps

## Making Theme Changes

1. Create a feature branch
   ```
   git checkout -b feature/theme-update
   ```

2. Make changes to theme files in Cursor

3. Test changes locally (if possible)

4. Commit changes
   ```
   git add .
   git commit -m "Updated theme elements"
   ```

5. Push to GitHub
   ```
   git push -u origin feature/theme-update
   ```

6. Pull changes to WordPress Studio for testing
   (This will require setting up WordPress Studio with Git or manually copying files)

7. Once tested and approved, merge to main branch
   ```
   git checkout main
   git merge feature/theme-update
   git push origin main
   ```

## Adding a New Plugin

1. Create a feature branch
   ```
   git checkout -b feature/add-plugin-name
   ```

2. Install plugin in WordPress Studio

3. Export/copy plugin files to your Cursor workspace

4. Commit the new plugin
   ```
   git add .
   git commit -m "Added new plugin: plugin-name"
   ```

5. Push to GitHub
   ```
   git push -u origin feature/add-plugin-name
   ```

6. Test plugin functionality in WordPress Studio

7. Once tested and approved, merge to main branch
   ```
   git checkout main
   git merge feature/add-plugin-name
   git push origin main
   ```

## Updating WordPress Core

> Note: WordPress core updates should generally be performed in WordPress Studio first, then synchronized to your development environment.

1. Back up your site in WordPress Studio

2. Apply WordPress update in WordPress Studio

3. Test site functionality

4. Create a feature branch in Cursor
   ```
   git checkout -b update/wp-core-version
   ```

5. Copy updated core files from WordPress Studio to Cursor

6. Commit the changes
   ```
   git add .
   git commit -m "Updated WordPress core to version X.X.X"
   ```

7. Push to GitHub
   ```
   git push -u origin update/wp-core-version
   ```

8. Once verified, merge to main branch
   ```
   git checkout main
   git merge update/wp-core-version
   git push origin main
   ```